* APOLLO 11 AS FLOWN: A VIEW-1108 SCENARIO (A RUN DECK, IN 1969 TERMS).
*
* A scenario is one mission's data as one source tells it: this one is the
* mission as flown, from the post-flight reports.  A pre-flight nominal
* scenario for the same mission would be a second file, a reel of its own.
* One card per line.  A card starting with * is a comment.  Fields are
* KEY=VALUE; times are g.e.t. h:mm:ss.s from this mission's range zero.
* The mission's identity (name, range zero, landing site, launch pad) is in
* mission.scn beside this file.  Each scenario is a reel (tools/pack.py:
* mission.scn and this file), and the kernel's card reader (src/vdeck.f)
* loads one reel's decks at a time into its run tables (#26 slice 7e);
* tools/gen_data.py checks the same cards and builds the page's copy (the
* reel's page.json).  SRC is the card's source, for readers.
*
* Sources:
*   MR  Apollo 11 Mission Report, MSC-00171, November 1969.  NASA re-scan
*       https://www.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/static/apollo50th/pdf/A11_MissionReport.pdf
*       (printed page numbers).  Table 7-II, p. 7-9, gives latitudes as
*       geodetic for the Earth and selenographic for the Moon (Table 7-I,
*       p. 7-8); altitudes in n mi; flight-path angle and heading space-fixed.
*   SP  R. W. Orloff, Apollo by the Numbers, NASA SP-2000-4029 (printed pages).
*
* Card types:
*   SCENARIO ID= (1: each reel numbers its own)  NAME=  (the mission's
*            name comes from its MISSION card, mission.scn)
*   LEG      TYPE=CIRC|CONIC|LUNAR|LCONIC|TABLE  FROM= TO=  (g.e.t. span
*            it covers)  VEH=CSM|LM|SIVB  (the vehicle on it; default CSM;
*            an S-IVB leg gives the S-IVB a state where traj.f SIVST's
*            rules give it none: this scenario has none)
*     CIRC   Earth circular orbit through a state: T= LAT= LON= HDG=, orbit
*            altitude ALT= (n mi).  LATTYPE=GC geocentric, GD geodetic.
*     CONIC  Earth-centred conic from a state: T= LAT= LON= ALT= V= (ft/s)
*            FPA= HDG= (deg).
*     LUNAR  Moon circular orbit through two states, T= LAT= LON= and
*            TB= LATB= LONB= (selenographic), N= whole revolutions between
*            them, ALT= (n mi).  The plane and the mean motion come from
*            the two states.  ALTB= (n mi): the radius moves steadily from
*            ALT at T to ALTB at TB (default ALT, a circle).
*     LCONIC Moon-centred conic from a state: T= LAT= LON= (selenographic)
*            ALT= (n mi above the mean radius) V= (ft/s) FPA= (deg); its
*            horizontal direction lies in the plane of the CSM's lunar leg
*            at T (MR Table 7-II's lunar headings are not in a frame we can
*            use, as for the REF cards below).  Or, with DV= (ft/s) and
*            P= R= N= (as a BURN card's) and no state: the same vehicle's
*            previous leg at T (mid-burn) plus that impulse.
*     TABLE  states listed by the ROW cards that follow it (no FROM= TO=;
*            the rows' times give the span), LATTYPE= for all of them,
*            joined by cubic Hermite arcs (traj.f TABRV).  Before the
*            first row and after the last the vehicle stands at that
*            row's place on the turning Earth.
*   ROW      T= LAT= LON= ALT= (n mi above the ellipsoid) V= (ft/s) FPA=
*            HDG= (deg): space-fixed, or with VEL=EF relative to the
*            turning Earth.
*   EVENT    KIND= T=  (an event the kernel keys on; LIFTOFF is the launch from
*            the pad, LIFT the LM's lunar lift-off)
*   TIMELINE T= KIND= NAME=  (a row of the mission's timeline; see TIMELINE below)
*   BURNCUE  IGN= CUT= VEH= ENG=  (a main-engine firing between two TIMELINE
*            rows, named; see Burn cue at the end)
*
SCENARIO ID=1 NAME="AS FLOWN"
*
* The powered ascent: SP p. 103's ascent table, lift-off to S-IVB first
* cutoff, where the parking orbit takes over (its T row).  Before lift-off
* the CSM stands on the pad at the lift-off row's place (0.032 n mi up:
* the table's).  The arcs between rows are ours (TABRV).
LEG TYPE=TABLE LATTYPE=GC SRC="SP p. 103, Apollo 11 ascent phase table: geocentric latitude, altitude, space-fixed velocity, flight-path angle and heading"
ROW T=0:00:00.63 LAT=28.4470 LON=-80.6041 ALT=0.032 V=1340.7 FPA=0.06 HDG=90.00 SRC="SP p. 103, liftoff"
ROW T=0:01:06.30 LAT=28.4523 LON=-80.5853 ALT=4.236 V=2023.9 FPA=27.88 HDG=85.32 SRC="SP p. 103, Mach 1 achieved"
ROW T=0:01:23.00 LAT=28.4624 LON=-80.5499 ALT=7.326 V=2671.9 FPA=29.23 HDG=82.41 SRC="SP p. 103, maximum dynamic pressure"
ROW T=0:02:15.20 LAT=28.5739 LON=-80.1517 ALT=23.761 V=6492.8 FPA=22.957 HDG=76.315 SRC="SP p. 103, S-IC center engine cutoff; the book prints longitude -81.1517, which would put it 50 n mi west of the pad: -80.1517, ours, fits the row's range of 25.067 n mi"
ROW T=0:02:41.63 LAT=28.7007 LON=-79.6908 ALT=35.701 V=9068.6 FPA=19.114 HDG=75.439 SRC="SP p. 103, S-IC outboard engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:02:42.30 LAT=28.7046 LON=-79.6764 ALT=36.029 V=9100.6 FPA=19.020 HDG=75.436 SRC="SP p. 103, S-IC/S-II separation"
ROW T=0:07:40.62 LAT=30.9513 LON=-69.4309 ALT=97.280 V=18725.5 FPA=0.897 HDG=79.646 SRC="SP p. 103, S-II center engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:09:08.22 LAT=31.7089 LON=-64.1983 ALT=101.142 V=22690.8 FPA=0.619 HDG=82.396 SRC="SP p. 103, S-II outboard engine cutoff"
ROW T=0:09:09.00 LAT=31.7152 LON=-64.1467 ALT=101.175 V=22699.6 FPA=0.611 HDG=82.426 SRC="SP p. 103, S-II/S-IVB separation"
ROW T=0:11:39.33 LAT=32.4865 LON=-53.4588 ALT=103.202 V=25561.6 FPA=0.011 HDG=88.414 SRC="SP p. 103, S-IVB 1st burn cutoff"
*
* Earth parking orbit.  The S-IVB first cutoff state, geocentric latitude,
* on a circle at the mean of the MR's 100.7 by 99.2 n mi (p. 3-1), from
* that cutoff on (Earth orbit insertion, 10 s later, has no position in
* SP's table).
LEG TYPE=CIRC FROM=0:11:39.33 TO=2:44:16.2 T=0:11:39.33 LATTYPE=GC LAT=32.4865 LON=-53.4588 V=25561.6 FPA=0.011 HDG=88.414 ALT=99.95 SRC="SP p. 103 ascent table, S-IVB 1st burn cutoff: geocentric 32.4865 N, -53.4588 E, space-fixed velocity 25,561.6, flight-path angle 0.011, heading 88.414; orbit MR p. 3-1"
*
* Translunar coast: two conics, from translunar injection and from the
* first midcourse correction cutoff.  Earth only (no lunar gravity): ours.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=2:50:13.2 TO=26:44:58.7 T=2:50:13.2 LATTYPE=GD LAT=9.98 LON=-164.84 ALT=180.6 V=35546 FPA=7.37 HDG=60.07 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, translunar injection"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=26:44:58.7 TO=75:49:50.4 T=26:45:01.8 LATTYPE=GD LAT=6.00 LON=-11.17 ALT=109477.2 V=5010.0 FPA=76.88 HDG=120.87 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, first midcourse correction cutoff"
*
* Lunar orbit: after insertion (an ellipse, 169.7 by 60.0 n mi, SP p. 104,
* put on a circle through its two rows at their mean altitude: ours), after
* circularization, and after undocking.  Rows from MR Table 7-II; the
* revolution counts are ours, from the periods those rows imply (7113 s
* after circularization).
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=75:49:50.4 TO=80:11:36.8 T=75:55:48.0 LAT=0.16 LON=167.13 TB=80:11:36.8 LATB=-0.02 LONB=170.09 N=1 ALT=114.9 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, lunar orbit insertion cutoff and circularization ignition; altitude the mean of SP p. 104's 169.7 by 60.0 n mi"
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=80:11:36.8 TO=100:12:00.0 T=80:11:53.5 LAT=-0.02 LON=169.16 TB=100:12:00.0 LATB=1.11 LONB=116.21 N=10 ALT=62.2 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, circularization cutoff and undocking; altitude the mean of the two rows"
LEG TYPE=LUNAR FROM=100:12:00.0 TO=135:23:42.3 T=100:40:01.9 LAT=1.05 LON=31.41 TB=130:09:31.2 LATB=1.10 LONB=41.85 N=14 ALT=62.0 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, separation cutoff and ascent stage jettison; altitude the mean of the two rows"
*
* The LM after undocking (VEH=LM; traj.f LMSTAT gives its state outside
* these spans).  From the separation to descent orbit insertion, a circle
* through the separation cutoff row and the DOI ignition row, its radius
* moving from the CSM leg's 62.0 n mi to the DOI row's 56.4.  The
* separation burn was the CSM's (service module RCS, 1.4 ft/s, 5.2 s: MR
* Table 7-V p. 7-11), so at its cutoff the LM was within a few hundred
* feet of the CSM: we take the CSM's row and its leg's altitude for the
* LM (the row's own 62.5 would put the LM 3000 ft from the CSM at once),
* and LMSTAT blends the 300 ft separation offset into the leg over its
* first 300 s.  (Through the undocking row instead, the LM's leg starts
* 18 km from the CSM's; a conic through the DOI row misses the
* separation row by 21 km.)  The descent orbit, a conic through the PDI
* row, from DOI cutoff to PDI: it passes 2.7 km behind the DOI cutoff row
* and 4.7 km across it (the plane is the CSM's: LCST), 57.8 by 6.4 n mi.
* A conic from the DOI cutoff row instead (57.8 by 11.4) misses the PDI
* row by 21.6 km along track and 9.4 km in height; ours, we keep the
* first.  SP p. 104 and MR Table 7-V print the descent orbit's 58.5 by
* 7.8 n mi on the PDI row (our reading: one row low; MR section 5.1 has
* "a 60- by 8.2-mile orbit").  No state for the powered descent before
* LMDESC's last 600 s, nor for the powered ascent (none found).  After
* lunar orbit insertion, conics through MR Table 7-II's LM rows: the
* insertion row to CSI ignition (50.1 by 9.4 n mi; SP p. 104 48.0 by
* 9.4), the CSI cutoff row to CDH ignition (50.9 by 47.5; SP 49.3 by
* 45.7), the TPI ignition row back to CDH cutoff (no CDH row: 49.4 by
* 42.7; SP 47.4 by 42.1) and the TPI cutoff row to TPF (63.8 by 44.0;
* SP 61.7 by 43.7).  The two-body conics part where they meet: at CDH
* by 42 km, mostly along track (ours, accepted).  The TPF row is a
* check only (its altitude is unreadable on our copy).
LEG TYPE=LUNAR VEH=LM FROM=100:39:52.9 TO=101:36:14.0 T=100:40:01.9 LAT=1.05 LON=31.41 TB=101:36:14.0 LATB=-1.12 LONB=-140.20 N=0 ALT=62.0 ALTB=56.4 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, separation cutoff (1.05 N, 31.41 E; the CSM's, taken for the LM, at the CSM leg's 62.0 n mi, not the row's 62.5: ours) and descent orbit insertion ignition (1.12 S, 140.20 W, 56.4 n mi); from the CSM/LM separation ignition, SP p. 104 100:39:52.90"
LEG TYPE=LCONIC VEH=LM FROM=101:36:44.0 TO=102:33:05.0 T=102:33:05.0 LAT=1.02 LON=39.39 ALT=6.4 V=5564.9 FPA=0.03 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, powered descent initiation: 1.02 N, 39.39 E, 6.4 n mi, 5564.9 ft/s, 0.03 deg; from DOI cutoff 101:36:44.00, SP p. 104"
LEG TYPE=LCONIC VEH=LM FROM=124:29:15.7 TO=125:19:35.0 T=124:29:15.7 LAT=0.73 LON=12.99 ALT=10.0 V=5537.9 FPA=0.28 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, LM orbit insertion: 0.73 N, 12.99 E, 10.0 n mi, 5537.9 ft/s, 0.28 deg; to CSI ignition 125:19:35.00, SP p. 104"
LEG TYPE=LCONIC VEH=LM FROM=125:20:22.0 TO=126:17:49.6 T=125:20:22.0 LAT=-0.91 LON=-149.57 ALT=48.4 V=5376.6 FPA=0.09 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, coelliptic sequence initiation cutoff: 0.91 S, 149.57 W, 48.4 n mi, 5376.6 ft/s, 0.09 deg; to CDH ignition 126:17:49.6, MR Table 7-V p. 7-11"
LEG TYPE=LCONIC VEH=LM FROM=126:18:07.4 TO=127:03:51.8 T=127:03:51.8 LAT=-1.17 LON=-110.28 ALT=44.1 V=5391.5 FPA=-0.16 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, terminal phase initiation ignition: 1.17 S, 110.28 W, 44.1 n mi, 5391.5 ft/s, -0.16 deg; from CDH cutoff 126:18:07.40, SP p. 104"
LEG TYPE=LCONIC VEH=LM FROM=127:04:14.5 TO=127:46:09.8 T=127:04:14.5 LAT=-1.17 LON=-111.46 ALT=44.0 V=5413.2 FPA=-0.03 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, terminal phase initiation cutoff: 1.17 S, 111.46 W, 44.0 n mi, 5413.2 ft/s, -0.03 deg; to TPF ignition 127:46:09.80, SP p. 104"
*
* Transearth coast: conics from the second midcourse correction and from
* command module/service module separation, to entry interface.
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=135:26:13.7 TO=150:29:57.4 T=150:29:57.4 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-13.16 LON=-37.79 ALT=169087.2 V=4075.0 FPA=-80.34 HDG=129.30 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, second midcourse correction ignition"
LEG TYPE=CONIC FROM=150:30:07.4 TO=195:03:05.7 T=194:49:12.7 LATTYPE=GD LAT=-35.09 LON=122.54 ALT=1778.3 V=29615.5 FPA=-35.26 HDG=69.27 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, command module/service module separation"
*
* Entry, entry interface to splashdown.  The MR gives no state between
* them; a single arc from entry interface to the drogues stays above the
* ground (our run).  Under the parachutes the CM falls straight down
* (ours); the main parachutes' row is ours: no time for it in the MR, so
* the drogues' 24,000 ft plus Apollo 8's 51.1 s from drogue to main
* deployment (MR8 Table 3-I p. 3-4), at about 10,000 ft (ours, from the
* Apollo 8 crew's 10K call, Apollo 8 Flight Journal, day 6, 146:55:32).
* After splashdown the CM rides at the splash point.  Table 7-VII prints
* the drogue latitude as south; the landing was north (MR p. 7-5, 13-4).
LEG TYPE=TABLE LATTYPE=GD SRC="Apollo 11 entry: MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12 and the landing point, MR pp. 7-5 and 13-4"
ROW T=195:03:05.7 LAT=-3.19 LON=171.96 ALT=65.8 V=36194.4 FPA=-6.48 HDG=50.18 SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, entry interface (400 000 ft)"
ROW T=195:12:06.9 LAT=13.30 LON=-169.15 ALT=3.950 V=300 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, drogue deployment, onboard guidance position; 24,000 ft (3.950 n mi), the forward heat shield's jettison height before the drogues (Apollo 11 press kit, printed p. 90); falling at 300 ft/s, ours"
ROW T=195:12:58.0 LAT=13.30 LON=-169.15 ALT=1.646 V=30 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="main parachute deployment, ours (see above): 10,000 ft (1.646 n mi), then about 30 ft/s, the mean fall from there to the water"
ROW T=195:18:35 LAT=13.317 LON=-169.15 ALT=0 V=31 FPA=-90 HDG=0 VEL=EF SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-5, landing 195:18:35; MR p. 13-4, 13 deg 19 min N, 169 deg 9 min W (recovery forces); splashdown at 31 ft/s on three parachutes, Apollo 11 press kit printed p. 62"
*
* Events the kernel keys on.
EVENT KIND=TDATT T=3:09:20 SRC="Apollo 11 Flight Journal 002:54:09: S-IVB manoeuvre to separation attitude to be completed at plus 09 plus 20"
EVENT KIND=SEP T=3:17:04.6 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4 and Table 7-II p. 7-9: command module/S-IVB separation. SP p. 104 has CSM separated from S-IVB at 003:15:23.00 and 003:17:04.60 as the separation manoeuvre ignition"
EVENT KIND=APPR T=3:20:30 SRC="Our guess: start of the docking approach, between separation and Collins' I'm still quite a ways at 003:22:25 (Flight Journal)"
EVENT KIND=DOCK T=3:24:03.1 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4 and Table 7-II p. 7-9; SP p. 104 has 003:24:03.70"
EVENT KIND=UNDOCK T=100:12:00.0 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4"
EVENT KIND=TOUCH T=102:45:39.9 SRC="MR Table 3-I p. 3-4, lunar landing"
EVENT KIND=EI T=195:03:05.7 SRC="MR Table 7-VII p. 7-12, entry interface"
EVENT KIND=PTC T=10:58:19 SRC="Apollo 11 Flight Journal, 010:58:19, Collins: PTC is started now"
EVENT KIND=LMSEP T=100:39:52.9 SRC="SP p. 104, CSM/LM separation ignition 100:39:52.90; MR Table 7-V p. 7-11"
EVENT KIND=PDI T=102:33:05.01 SRC="SP p. 104, LM powered descent initiation 102:33:05.01"
EVENT KIND=LIFT T=124:22:00.79 SRC="SP p. 104, LM lunar liftoff ignition 124:22:00.79"
EVENT KIND=TPF T=127:46:09.8 SRC="SP p. 104, LM terminal phase finalize ignition 127:46:09.80"
EVENT KIND=LMDOK T=128:03:00.0 SRC="SP p. 104, CSM/LM docked 128:03:00.00; MR Table 7-II p. 7-9"
EVENT KIND=JETT T=130:09:31.2 SRC="SP p. 104, LM ascent stage jettisoned 130:09:31.20; MR Table 7-II p. 7-9"
EVENT KIND=CMSEP T=194:49:12.7 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, command module/service module separation; SP p. 109 has 194:49:12.70"
*
* The launch vehicle's stages (vdrive.f LVPL, ASCPL; #97): the stack stands on
* the mobile launcher at the pad before lift-off, then drops the S-IC, the
* launch escape tower and the S-II at these rows of the timeline below.
EVENT KIND=LIFTOFF T=0:00:00.63 SRC="SP p. 105, Liftoff (umbilical disconnected) 000:00:00.63"
EVENT KIND=SICSEP T=0:02:42.30 SRC="SP p. 105, S-IC maximum Earth-fixed velocity. S-IC/S-II separation command 000:02:42.30"
EVENT KIND=LESJET T=0:03:17.90 SRC="SP p. 105, Launch escape tower jettisoned 000:03:17.90"
EVENT KIND=SIISEP T=0:09:09.00 SRC="SP p. 105, S-II maximum Earth-fixed velocity. S-II/S-IVB separation command 000:09:09.00"
*
* The S-IVB (traj.f SIVST): with the CSM to SEP, scene 7's geometry to the
* spacecraft's ejection, then the CSM's state less the separation the CSM
* made: the ejection springs' "about one fps" (Apollo 11 press kit, printed
* p. 30) and the evasive manoeuvre (the BURN card at 4:40:03.25 below), to
* the first event of the slingshot, after which we have no state for it:
* MR p. 15-1 gives the slingshot's means (a liquid oxygen dump, an
* auxiliary propulsion system firing and liquid hydrogen venting) and its
* closest approach, "1825 miles above the lunar surface" at 78:42:00, but
* no velocity change.
EVENT KIND=EJECT T=4:16:59.1 SRC="MR Table 7-II p. 7-9, spacecraft/S-IVB separation (ejection); SP p. 106 has CSM/LM ejected from S-IVB 004:17:03.00"
EVENT KIND=SLING T=4:51:07.7 SRC="SP p. 106, S-IVB lunar slingshot maneuver-LH2 tank CVS opened 004:51:07.70, the first of the slingshot's timeline rows after the manoeuvre to its attitude (MR p. 15-1: liquid hydrogen venting was one of the slingshot's three means)"
*
* ---------------------------------------------------------------------
* TIMELINE: the mission's sequence of events as SP-4029 prints it (printed pp. 105-110, "Apollo 11 Timeline"),
* one card per row, in the book's order, for chapter marks and the scenes
* to key on.  T is the book's g.e.t. (negative before range zero), NAME its
* wording (OCR slips mended, quotation marks made ', cut to 60 characters
* with ...), SRC its page.  KIND is ours, one of (CLAUDE.md, "Scenario
* timeline"): LAUNCH countdown, lift-off and ascent flight; BURN a firing,
* ignition or cutoff (S-IVB, SPS, RCS, LM); STAGING launch-vehicle stage
* events (engine cutoffs, separations, jettisons, apex, impact); ORBIT
* orbit and trajectory milestones; SEP spacecraft separation, docking,
* undocking, ejection, jettison; SURFACE on the Moon, landing to lunar
* lift-off; TV television; CREW crew and CAPCOM words, crew movements;
* PHOTO photography and sightings; ENTRY entry, landing and recovery; MARK
* anything else (systems, communications, venting).  The EVENT cards above
* stay the kernel's keys.
*
TIMELINE T=-028:00:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Terminal countdown started" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-009:00:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Scheduled 11-hour hold at T-9 hours" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-009:00:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Countdown resumed at T-9 hours" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-003:30:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Scheduled 1-hour 32-minute hold at T-3 hours 30 minutes" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-003:30:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Countdown resumed at T-3 hours 30 minutes" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:16.968 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Guidance reference release" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:08.90 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="S-IC engine start command" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:06.40 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="S-IC engine ignition (#5)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=-000:00:01.60 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="All S-IC engines thrust OK" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Range zero" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.30 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="All holddown arms released (1st motion)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:00.63 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Liftoff (umbilical disconnected) (1.07 g)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:01.70 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Tower clearance yaw maneuver started" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:09.70 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Yaw maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:13.20 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Pitch and roll maneuver started" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:00:31.10 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Roll maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:01:06.30 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Mach 1 achieved" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:01:23.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Maximum dynamic pressure (735.17 lb/ft2)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:01:31.50 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Maximum bending moment (33,200,000 lbf-in)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:15.20 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC center engine cutoff command" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:40.00 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Pitch maneuver ended" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:41.63 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC outboard engine cutoff" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:41.71 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC maximum total inertial acceleration (3.94 g)" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:42.30 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-IC maximum Earth-fixed velocity. S-IC/S-II separation..." SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:43.04 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II engine start command" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:02:44.00 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II ignition" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:03:12.30 KIND=STAGING NAME="S-II aft interstage jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:03:17.90 KIND=STAGING NAME="Launch escape tower jettisoned" SRC="SP p. 105"
TIMELINE T=000:03:24.10 KIND=LAUNCH NAME="Iterative guidance mode initiated" SRC="SP p. 105"
